**[Only relevant if you run gundeck with its default Redis presence
store]** Storing presence data in Redis is deprecated; PostgreSQL is
now supported as gundeck's presence store and will become the default
in a future release, at which point Redis support will be removed.

To migrate: set the helm value `gundeck.presenceStore: postgresql` and
configure `gundeck.config.postgresql` (values in libpq format) plus
`gundeck.config.postgresqlPool`; the password can be set via
`gundeck.secrets.pgPassword`.  Gundeck creates the `presence` table on
startup; no data migration is needed, presences are re-registered as
clients reconnect.  The `redis-ephemeral` release, its TLS
certificates and gundeck's `redis` settings become unnecessary.

If you do nothing, gundeck keeps using Redis for now.

See
https://docs.wire.com/latest/how-to/install/infrastructure-configuration.html#gundeck-presence-store
